          <row><cell>Ormond Dancing Academy</cell><cell><ref target="civic?id=Madeline%20Street">Madeline Street</ref></cell><cell>3</cell><cell>1900</cell></row>
          <row><cell>Hayes, Miss Mary, ladies' college</cell><cell><ref target="civic?id=Leicester%20Street">Leicester Street</ref></cell><cell>216</cell><cell>1900</cell></row>
          <row><cell>Halsall, Mrs E., music teacher</cell><cell><ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref></cell><cell>176</cell><cell>1940</cell></row>
          <row><cell>Merlyn, Miss M., dancing teacher</cell><cell><ref target="civic?id=Swanston%20Street">Swanston Street</ref></cell><cell>616</cell><cell>1940</cell></row>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Notes</head>
        <list rend="bulleted">
          <item>The University, the Training College (later the Teachers' College), University High School and the medical, law and engineering schools are listed on the north side of <ref target="civic?id=Grattan%20Street">Grattan Street</ref>, and Trinity and Ormond colleges in Sydney Road. All of them are in the University grounds, outside the project area.</item>
          <item>St Matthew's School appears under Queensberry Street in 1857 and 1858, in the early alphabetical lists, which give no address. It isn't known whether it was in the project area.</item>
          <item>A Baptist Sunday school is listed with the Baptist mission hall in Bouverie Street from 1915 to 1940 (see <ref target="civic?id=Churches">Churches</ref>).</item>
        </list>
        <p>Every listing can be browsed in <ref target="search?q=school&amp;src=directories">search</ref>.</p>
      </div>
    </body>
